      "domain": "election_polling",
      "title": "election polling method",
      "summary": "In an election poll, 95 of 100 sampled voters favored a measure. To obtain a 95% lower confidence bound for the underlying favorable proportion, analysts used the Wilson score lower endpoint: (p + z^2/(2n) - z*sqrt(p(1-p)/n + z^2/(4n^2))) / (1 + z^2/n), with z=1.96. They compared that lower endpoint, not p alone, with the required support floor.",
      "signature": {
        "goal": [
          "solve analogous estimation or decision"
        ],
        "constraints": [
          "use observed quantities"
        ],
        "failed_predictions": [
          "surface value alone is sufficient"
